      <field>
       <name>send_auto_stop</name>
       <description>When set, SD/MMC sends stop command to SD_MMC_CEATA cards at end of data transfer. Determine the following:
*-when send_auto_stop bit should be set, since some data   transfers do not need explicit stop commands. *-open-ended transfers that software should explicitly   send to stop command.
Additionally, when resume is sent to resume- suspended memory access of SD-Combo card, bit should be set correctly if suspended data transfer needs send_auto_stop. Don't care if no data expected from card.</description>
       <lsb>12</lsb>
       <msb>12</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>sdmmc_cmd_send_auto_stop_enum</name>
