      <field>
       <name>stop_abort_cmd</name>
       <description>When open-ended or predefined data transfer is in progress, and host issues stop or abort command to stop data transfer, bit should be set so that command/data state-machines of CIU can return correctly to idle state. This is also applicable for Boot mode transfers. To Abort boot mode, this bit should be set along with CMD[26] = disable_boot.
 Note: If abort is sent to function-number currently selected or not in data-transfer mode, then bit should be set to 0.</description>
       <lsb>14</lsb>
       <msb>14</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
