  <peripheral>
   <name>l3regs</name>
   <version>0.0</version>
   <description>Registers to control L3 interconnect settings</description>
   <baseAddress>0xff800000</baseAddress>
   <access>read-write</access>
   <addressBlock>
    <offset>0x0</offset>
    <size>0x4c10c</size>
    <usage>registers</usage>
   </addressBlock>
   <registers>
    <register>
     <name>remap</name>
     <description>The L3 interconnect has separate address maps for the various L3 Masters. Generally, the addresses are the same for most masters. However, the sparse interconnect of the L3 switch causes some masters to have holes in their memory maps. The remap bits are not mutually exclusive. Each bit can be set independently and in combinations. Priority for the bits is determined by the bit offset: lower offset bits take precedence over higher offset bits.</description>
     <addressOffset>0x0</addressOffset>
     <size>32</size>
     <access>write-only</access>
     <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
     <resetMask>0xffffffff</resetMask>
     <fields>
      <field>
       <name>mpuzero</name>
       <description>Controls whether address 0x0 for the MPU L3 master is mapped to the Boot ROM or On-chip RAM.  This field only has an effect on the MPU L3 master.</description>
       <lsb>0</lsb>
       <msb>0</msb>
       <access>write-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>l3regs_remap_mpuzero_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>bootrom</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>ocram</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>nonmpuzero</name>
       <description>Controls whether address 0x0 for the non-MPU L3 masters is mapped to the SDRAM or On-chip RAM.  This field only has an effect on the non-MPU L3 masters. The non-MPU L3 masters are the DMA controllers (standalone and those built-in to peripherals), the FPGA2HPS AXI Bridge, and the DAP.</description>
       <lsb>1</lsb>
       <msb>1</msb>
       <access>write-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>l3regs_remap_nonmpuzero_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>sdram</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>ocram</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>hps2fpga</name>
       <description>Controls whether the HPS2FPGA AXI Bridge is visible to L3 masters or not.</description>
       <lsb>3</lsb>
       <msb>3</msb>
       <access>write-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>l3regs_remap_hps2fpga_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>invisible</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>visible</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>lwhps2fpga</name>
       <description>Controls whether the Lightweight HPS2FPGA AXI Bridge is visible to L3 masters or not.</description>
       <lsb>4</lsb>
       <msb>4</msb>
       <access>write-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>l3regs_remap_lwhps2fpga_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>invisible</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>visible</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
     </fields>
    </register>
