      </field>
     </fields>
    </register>
    <register>
     <name>hostgrp_hcint7</name>
     <description>This register indicates the status of a channel with respect to USB- and AHB-related events. The application must read this register when the Host Channels Interrupt bit of the Core Interrupt register (GINTSTS.HChInt) is set. Before the application can read this register, it must first read the Host All Channels Interrupt (HAINT) register to get the exact channel number for the Host Channel-n Interrupt register. The application must clear the appropriate bit in this register to clear the corresponding bits in the HAINT and GINTSTS registers.</description>
     <addressOffset>0x5e8</addressOffset>
     <size>32</size>
     <access>read-only</access>
     <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
     <resetMask>0xffffffff</resetMask>
     <fields>
      <field>
       <name>xfercompl</name>
       <description>Transfer completed normally without any errors. This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>0</lsb>
       <msb>0</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_xfercompl_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>chhltd</name>
       <description>In non Scatter/Gather DMA mode, it indicates the transfer completed abnormally either because of any USB transaction error or in response to disable request by the application or because of a completed transfer. In Scatter/gather DMA mode, this indicates that transfer completed due to any of the following
. EOL being set in descriptor
. AHB error
. Excessive transaction errors
. Babble
. Stall</description>
       <lsb>1</lsb>
       <msb>1</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_chhltd_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>ahberr</name>
       <description>This is generated only in Internal DMA mode when there is an AHB error during AHB read/write. The application can read the corresponding channel's DMA address register to get the error address.</description>
       <lsb>2</lsb>
       <msb>2</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_ahberr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>stall</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core. This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>3</lsb>
       <msb>3</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_stall_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>nak</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core.This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>4</lsb>
       <msb>4</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_nak_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>ack</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core. This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>5</lsb>
       <msb>5</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_ack_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>nyet</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core.This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>6</lsb>
       <msb>6</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_nyet_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>xacterr</name>
       <description>Indicates one of the following errors occurred on the USB.-CRC check failure
-Timeout
-Bit stuff error
-False EOP
In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core. This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>7</lsb>
       <msb>7</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_xacterr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>bblerr</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core..This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>8</lsb>
       <msb>8</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_bblerr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>frmovrun</name>
       <description>In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core. This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it.</description>
       <lsb>9</lsb>
       <msb>9</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_frmovrun_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>datatglerr</name>
       <description>This bit can be set only by the core and the application should write 1 to clear it. In Scatter/Gather DMA mode, the interrupt due to this bit is masked in the core.</description>
       <lsb>10</lsb>
       <msb>10</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_datatglerr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>bnaintr</name>
       <description>This bit is valid only when Scatter/Gather DMA mode is enabled. The core generates this interrupt when the descriptor accessed is not ready for the Core to process. BNA will not be generated for Isochronous channels. for non Scatter/Gather DMA mode, this bit is reserved.</description>
       <lsb>11</lsb>
       <msb>11</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_bnaintr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>xcs_xact_err</name>
       <description>This bit is valid only when Scatter/Gather DMA mode is enabled. The core sets this bit when 3 consecutive transaction errors occurred on the USB bus. XCS_XACT_ERR will not be generated for Isochronous channels.for non Scatter/Gather DMA mode, this bit is reserved.</description>
       <lsb>12</lsb>
       <msb>12</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_xcs_xact_err_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>acvtive</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>desc_lst_rollintr</name>
       <description>Descriptor rollover interrupt (DESC_LST_ROLLIntr)This bit is valid only when Scatter/Gather DMA mode is enabled. The core sets this bit when the corresponding channel's descriptor list rolls over. for non Scatter/Gather DMA mode, this bit is reserved.</description>
       <lsb>13</lsb>
       <msb>13</msb>
       <access>read-only</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcint7_desc_lst_rollintr_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>inactive</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>active</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
     </fields>
    </register>
    <register>
     <name>hostgrp_hcintmsk7</name>
     <description>This register reflects the mask for each channel status described in the previous section.</description>
     <addressOffset>0x5ec</addressOffset>
     <size>32</size>
     <access>read-write</access>
     <resetValue>0x0</resetValue>
     <resetMask>0xffffffff</resetMask>
     <fields>
      <field>
       <name>xfercomplmsk</name>
       <description>Transfer complete.</description>
       <lsb>0</lsb>
       <msb>0</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcintmsk7_xfercomplmsk_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>mask</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>nomask</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>chhltdmsk</name>
       <description>Channel Halted.</description>
       <lsb>1</lsb>
       <msb>1</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcintmsk7_chhltdmsk_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>mask</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>nomask</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>ahberrmsk</name>
       <description>In  scatter/gather DMA  mode  for  host, interrupts will not be generated due to the corresponding bits set in HCINTn.</description>
       <lsb>2</lsb>
       <msb>2</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcintmsk7_ahberrmsk_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>mask</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>nomask</name>
          <value>1</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
       </enumeratedValues>
      </field>
      <field>
       <name>bnaintrmsk</name>
       <description>This bit is valid only when Scatter/Gather DMA mode is enabled.</description>
       <lsb>11</lsb>
       <msb>11</msb>
       <access>read-write</access>
       <enumeratedValues>
        <name>usb_hostgrp_hcintmsk7_bnaintrmsk_enum</name>
         <enumeratedValue>
          <name>mask</name>
          <value>0</value>
         </enumeratedValue>
